               </link> - 
Bean Property Type for the <code>service.vendor</code> service property.
   </para>
         </listitem>
      </itemizedlist>
   </section>
   <section xreflabel="BeanPropertyException"
            role="class"
            xml:id="org.osgi.service.cdi.propertytypes.BeanPropertyException">
      <title>public class BeanPropertyException<?line-break?> extends RuntimeException</title>
      <para>
This Runtime Exception is thrown when a Bean Property Type method attempts an
 invalid component property coercion. For example when the bean property type
 method <code>Long test();</code> is applied to a component property <code>"test"</code>
 of type String.
   </para>
      <section xreflabel="BeanPropertyException(String)"
               role="method"
               xml:id="org.osgi.service.cdi.propertytypes.BeanPropertyException.BeanPropertyException-String-">
         <title>public  BeanPropertyException(String message)</title>
         <formalpara role="parameter">
            <title>message</title>
            <para>The message for this exception.</para>
         </formalpara>
         <para role="description">
Create a Bean Property Exception with a message.
   </para>
      </section>
      <section xreflabel="BeanPropertyException(String,Throwable)"
               role="method"
               xml:id="org.osgi.service.cdi.propertytypes.BeanPropertyException.BeanPropertyException-String-Throwable-">
         <title>public  BeanPropertyException(String message, Throwable cause)</title>
         <formalpara role="parameter">
            <title>message</title>
            <para>The message for this exception.</para>
         </formalpara>
         <formalpara role="parameter">
            <title>cause</title>
            <para>The causing exception.</para>
         </formalpara>
         <para role="description">
Create a Bean Property Exception with a message and a nested cause.
   </para>
      </section>
   </section>
   <section xreflabel="ExportedService"
            role="class"
            xml:id="org.osgi.service.cdi.propertytypes.ExportedService">
      <title>@ExportedService</title>
      <para>
Bean Property Type for the remote service properties for an exported service.
 </para>
      <para>
 This annotation can be used as defined by <link linkend="org.osgi.service.cdi.annotations.BeanPropertyType">BeanPropertyType</link> to declare
 the values of the remote service properties for an exported service.</para>
      <formalpara role="parameter">
         <title>See Also</title>
         <para>
            <code>Bean Property Types</code>, <code>Remote Services Specification</code>
         </para>
      </formalpara>
      <formalpara role="parameter">
         <title>Retention</title>
         <para>
            <code>RUNTIME</code>
         </para>
      </formalpara>
      <formalpara role="parameter">
         <title>Target</title>
         <para>
            <code>FIELD</code>, <code>METHOD</code>, <code>PARAMETER</code>, <code>TYPE</code>
         </para>
      </formalpara>
      <section xreflabel="service_exported_interfaces"
               role="method"
               xml:id="org.osgi.service.cdi.propertytypes.ExportedService.service_exported_interfaces--">
         <title>Class&lt;?&gt;[] service_exported_interfaces</title>
         <para role="description">
Service property marking the service for export. It defines the
 interfaces under which the service can be exported.
 </para>
         <para>
 If an empty array is specified, the property is not added to the
 component description.</para>
         <formalpara role="parameter">
            <title>Returns</title>
            <para>The exported service interfaces.</para>
         </formalpara>
         <formalpara role="parameter">
            <title>See Also</title>
            <para>
               <link linkend="org.osgi.framework.Constants.SERVICE_EXPORTED_INTERFACES">Constants.SERVICE_EXPORTED_INTERFACES</link>
            </para>
         </formalpara>
      </section>
      <section xreflabel="service_exported_configs"
               role="method"
               xml:id="org.osgi.service.cdi.propertytypes.ExportedService.service_exported_configs--">
         <title>String[] service_exported_configs default {}</title>
         <para role="description">
Service property identifying the configuration types that should be used
 to export the service.
 </para>
         <para>
 If an empty array is specified, the default value, the property is not
 added to the component description.</para>
         <formalpara role="parameter">
            <title>Returns</title>
            <para>The configuration types.</para>
         </formalpara>
         <formalpara role="parameter">
            <title>See Also</title>
            <para>
               <link linkend="org.osgi.framework.Constants.SERVICE_EXPORTED_CONFIGS">Constants.SERVICE_EXPORTED_CONFIGS</link>
            </para>
         </formalpara>
      </section>
      <section xreflabel="service_exported_intents"
               role="method"
               xml:id="org.osgi.service.cdi.propertytypes.ExportedService.service_exported_intents--">
         <title>String[] service_exported_intents default {}</title>
         <para role="description">
Service property identifying the intents that the distribution provider
 must implement to distribute the service.
 </para>
         <para>
 If an empty array is specified, the default value, the property is not
 added to the component description.</para>
         <formalpara role="parameter">
            <title>Returns</title>
            <para>The intents that the distribution provider must implement to
         distribute the service.</para>
         </formalpara>
         <formalpara role="parameter">
            <title>See Also</title>
            <para>
               <link linkend="org.osgi.framework.Constants.SERVICE_EXPORTED_INTENTS">Constants.SERVICE_EXPORTED_INTENTS</link>
            </para>
         </formalpara>
      </section>
      <section xreflabel="service_exported_intents_extra"
               role="method"
               xml:id="org.osgi.service.cdi.propertytypes.ExportedService.service_exported_intents_extra--">
         <title>String[] service_exported_intents_extra default {}</title>
         <para role="description">
Service property identifying the extra intents that the distribution
 provider must implement to distribute the service.
 </para>
         <para>
 If an empty array is specified, the default value, the property is not
 added to the component description.</para>
         <formalpara role="parameter">
            <title>Returns</title>
            <para>The extra intents that the distribution provider must implement
         to distribute the service.</para>
         </formalpara>
         <formalpara role="parameter">
            <title>See Also</title>
            <para>
               <link linkend="org.osgi.framework.Constants.SERVICE_EXPORTED_INTENTS_EXTRA">Constants.SERVICE_EXPORTED_INTENTS_EXTRA</link>
            </para>
         </formalpara>
      </section>
      <section xreflabel="service_intents"
               role="method"
               xml:id="org.osgi.service.cdi.propertytypes.ExportedService.service_intents--">
         <title>String[] service_intents default {}</title>
         <para role="description">
Service property identifying the intents that this service implements.
 </para>
         <para>
 If an empty array is specified, the default value, the property is not
 added to the component description.</para>
         <formalpara role="parameter">
            <title>Returns</title>
            <para>The intents that the service implements.</para>
         </formalpara>
         <formalpara role="parameter">
            <title>See Also</title>
            <para>
               <link linkend="org.osgi.framework.Constants.SERVICE_INTENTS">Constants.SERVICE_INTENTS</link>
            </para>
         </formalpara>
      </section>
   </section>
